WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.040
Local neural programs compiled from English descriptions now run entirely on CPU without external APIs. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 179. Program as weights lets users describe a text function in English and compile it into a reusable neural program. The system relies on a fine-tuned Q3-4B to generate a LLHF adapter for a frozen Q3-0.6B interpreter.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:32.600
On Fuzzy Bench, the approach hits 73.4% exact match accuracy.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.980
Compolation stays separate from inference, so the task definition remains fixed while

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:38.820
inputs vary.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:42.640
The project releases code and model weights as open source.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:48.960
A higher accuracy path called compile by training runs 100 steps of adapter fine-tuning

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.900
and reaches 83.6% semantic accuracy on Fuzzy Bench hard.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:01:00.120
The interpreter stays frozen in every case, so only the generated adapter changes per task.

